  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A closer approach to nonlinear escalation thresholds raises market risk premia and speculative bids on oil as markets price a higher probability of major supply disruptions, pushing benchmark crude prices upward.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">gulf_maritime_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
