<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::us_executive_policy_towa" target="global_energy_supply_sho::crude_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A more restrictive U.S. executive stance (tighter sanctions, export controls or embargo-related measures) reduces accessible Russian crude to world markets and/or increases risk premia, lifting benchmark crude prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::us_executive_policy_towa" target="gulf_maritime_escalation::materiel_intel_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A U.S. executive decision to prioritize resources for the Ukraine campaign (more restrictive orientation toward reallocating support) results in reduced weapons, munitions and intelligence transfers or slower replenishment to Gulf partners and proxies.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">gulf_maritime_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::us_executive_policy_towa" target="us_china_tech_trade_riva::regulatory_scrutiny_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A more restrictive executive foreign‑policy orientation in response to the war drives agencies and the administration to propose stricter AI oversight, tighter vendor vetting and expanded enforcement priorities, increasing regulatory scrutiny of AI activities and partners.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade_riva</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::us_executive_policy_towa" target="western_alliance_fragili::donor_ad_spend_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A shift in the US executive toward greater permissiveness with the adversary triggers immediate mobilization by major donors (especially hawkish or industry-aligned donors) to fund targeted ad campaigns for or against incumbents to alter policy, raising ad spend flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">western_alliance_fragili</data>
</edge>
