<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::allied_cohesion_level" target="gulf_maritime_escalation::escalation_proximity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher cohesion among U.S. and partner states produces coordinated naval patrols, joint deterrent postures and unified sanctions/diplomatic pressure that reduce the likelihood of maritime provocations crossing escalation triggers in the Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">gulf_maritime_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::allied_cohesion_level" target="us_china_tech_trade_riva::capital_flow_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger allied coordination produces joint public investment vehicles, coordinated subsidy and procurement strategies and investor guidance that channel public and private capital toward allied AI firms and infrastructure, raising net capital flows into those AI assets.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade_riva</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::allied_cohesion_level" target="western_alliance_fragili::messaging_coherence" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher allied cohesion produces coordinated talking points, shared information releases and synchronized policy signals that campaign actors and government spokespeople echo, increasing public messaging alignment; the reverse (allied splits) produces divergent narratives and incoherent messages.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">western_alliance_fragili</data>
</edge>
