<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::crude_price_level" target="gulf_maritime_escalation::escalation_proximity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained increases in crude prices raise Gulf state and non‑state actor revenues and fiscal space, enabling greater military sustainment and proxy support which directly moves the system closer to nonlinear escalation thresholds as actors can afford higher-risk operations.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">gulf_maritime_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::crude_price_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::us_executive_policy_towa" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained increases in global crude prices create domestic economic and political pressure (industry, consumers, allied partners) that push the executive toward more permissive or conciliatory policy moves to restore supplies and lower prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::crude_price_level" target="us_china_tech_trade_riva::market_price_ai_assets" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained spike in crude raises energy and transport costs and increases macro risk/inflation expectations, compressing margins and discount rates for capital‑intensive tech firms and prompting investors to mark down valuations of AI infrastructure and chipmakers.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade_riva</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::crude_price_level" target="western_alliance_fragili::donor_ad_spend_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained higher benchmark crude prices raise producer and exporter revenues and predictable cashflow, prompting energy-sector and allied major donors to increase targeted ad spending to shape regulatory and fiscal policy.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">western_alliance_fragili</data>
</edge>
