  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp increases in diesel prices raise transport and agricultural costs, provoking strikes, supply-disruption protests, and rural/urban backlash that can fracture governing coalitions or force executive personnel changes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
